# Every text file is stored and checked out with line feeds.
#
# `core.autocrlf=input` reaches the same result, and it is a setting of the machine rather than
# of the repository: it holds until the first checkout made without it. A file saved with
# carriage returns then reaches a generator that copies bytes. `scripts/sync-docs.mjs` mirrors
# `CHANGELOG.md` and the extension README onto site pages and puts its own frontmatter, written
# with line feeds, at the head of each. The page then goes to a public repository with both
# endings in it. `newline=""` in the Python generators does not reach that far. It says how a
# file is written and says nothing about what was inside the file that was read.
#
# `text=auto` leaves it to git to tell text from binary, and `eol=lf` says how the text ones
# are checked out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Sources are text, whatever byte ends up inside a string literal.
#
# git decides "text or binary" by looking for a NUL in the first kilobytes of the file. A control
# character used on purpose - a NUL as the separator of a composite key, say - is enough to turn
# the whole file binary: the diff collapses to "Bin 0 -> 13641 bytes", and hundreds of lines pass
# review, the language checks and the release notes unseen. The `diff` attribute states the type
# outright and brings the line diff back.
#
# `diff` is all these lines set. The line ending of the same files comes from the rule above.
*.py    diff
*.ts    diff
*.js    diff
*.mjs   diff
*.json  diff
*.md    diff
*.txt   diff
*.toml  diff
*.cfg   diff
*.yaml  diff
*.yml   diff
*.xbsl  diff
*.css   diff
*.html  diff
*.svg   diff
*.cmd   diff

# Binaries stay binary: git must not try to read them as lines, nor touch their bytes. They are
# named here even though `text=auto` guesses them right today, because a guess is a fine default
# and a poor promise. Pictures and fonts are in the repository now; the other three types are
# named before the first such file arrives.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.woff2 binary
*.vsix  binary
*.zip   binary
